---
components: ["CommandPalette"]
description: Command palettes let users find and run commands, jump to pages and change settings from the keyboard, without leaving what they are doing.
---

## Basic

Pass the commands as `items`, each with a unique id and display text, and bind `open`. Focus moves to the search field when the palette opens and returns to the trigger when it closes. The first match is highlighted, so <DocKbd label="Enter" /> runs it. The arrow keys move the highlight, <DocKbd label="Page Up" /> and <DocKbd label="Page Down" /> move it by ten, and <DocKbd label="Escape" /> or a click outside closes the palette.

Listen for `select` to run a command. Its detail holds the command's id and item. The palette closes after it; call `event.preventDefault()` to keep it open. The query clears on close.

Carbon has no command palette. This one follows Carbon's modal, search and list box patterns, is marked experimental, and its API may change in a minor release.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPalette" />

## Sizes

Set `size` to control the height of the search field and the rows. The default is `"md"`, 40px. `"sm"` is 32px and `"lg"` is 48px.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteSizes" />

## Item data

Commands can keep the shape your data already has. Set `itemToId`, `itemToString` and `itemToGroup` to read the id, the label and the group from each item. The palette does not change the items, and `select` passes back the item you gave it.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteAccessors" />

## Matching

Typing filters the commands with fuzzy matching and ranks the best matches first: a prefix, then a word start, then a match inside a word, then scattered letters. Matched characters are emphasized. A description matches only when it holds the query as one run, so scattered letters in long text don't pull in unrelated commands. Add `keywords` to match terms that the label does not show. Screen readers hear the number of results once the user stops typing.

Pass `match` to change how text is matched. It receives the text and the query and returns whether it matched, an optional score and the indices to emphasize. Return no indices to drop the emphasis.

Labels and descriptions wrap. On small screens the key caps are hidden first, so the label keeps the row.

## Groups

Set `group` on items to show them under a header, or read the group with `itemToGroup`. Ungrouped items come first. While the user types, each group moves by its best match. Use the `group` slot to render the header yourself.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteGroups" />

## Keyboard shortcuts

Set `shortcut` on an item to show its keys, such as `"mod+shift+d"`. `mod` reads <DocKbd label="⌘" /> on macOS and iOS and <DocKbd label="Ctrl" /> elsewhere. The option names the keys in `aria-keyshortcuts`. The palette shows shortcuts but does not run them, and it adds no listener to the page.

To open the palette from anywhere, call `onShortcut` in `onMount`. It returns the function that removes the listener, so `onMount` cleans it up. Nothing listens until you call it. A shortcut without a modifier, such as <DocKbd label="/" />, does not fire while the user types in a field. Show the shortcut next to your trigger with [Kbd](/components/Kbd).

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteShortcuts" />

## Links

Set `href` on an item to render it as a link. Selecting it follows the link, and a modifier click opens a new tab. For a client-side router, call `event.preventDefault()` in `select` and navigate yourself.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteLinks" />

## Custom rows

Use the default slot to render a row's content. The slot receives the `item`, whether it is `highlighted`, and the label's `segments`, each with its text and whether it matched.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteCustomRow" />

## Empty states

Set `noResultsText` to the message shown when nothing matches the query, or pass a function to build it from the query. Set `emptyText` to the message shown when there are no commands at all. Use the `noResults` and `empty` slots for richer content.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteEmpty" />

## Footer

Use the `footer` slot for hints or secondary actions under the results.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteFooter" />

## Layering

The palette starts a [Layer](/components/Layer) wherever it renders, like a modal, so it looks the same when it opens from a layered surface. It stacks above an open [Modal](/components/Modal), whatever their order on the page.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteLayer" />

## Width

The palette is 640px wide, or the window width on small screens. Set the `--ccs-command-palette-width` custom property to change it, for all palettes with `:root { --ccs-command-palette-width: 48rem; }` or for one with `<CommandPalette --ccs-command-palette-width="48rem">`.

## Right-to-left

Inside a `dir="rtl"` page or a [LayoutDirection](/components/LayoutDirection), the icons, the highlight bar and the keys move to the other side. The keys keep their left-to-right order, as platform menus show them. To render the palette outside a transformed container, wrap it in a [Portal](/components/Portal), which keeps the direction and the [ThemeZone](/components/ThemeZone) theme.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteRtl" />

## Async results

For results from a server, set `shouldFilter` to `false` and update `items` on `search`. Set `debounce` to wait for a pause in typing before `search` fires; the field and the emphasis still update on every key. Set `loading` while the request runs. The list is marked busy at once, and `loadingDelay` holds the loading row back so fast responses show none.

Drop a response that a newer search replaced. When a search fails, keep the results you have and show the error with a retry button in the `footer` slot. In this example, a query with "cron" fails.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteAsync" />

## Large lists

Above 100 items, the palette renders only the rows in view. Set `virtualize` to `false` to render every row, or pass an object to tune it, as in [ComboBox](/components/ComboBox#virtualization).

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteVirtualized" />
